---
import Base from "../../layouts/Base.astro";
import { pageIntroductions } from "../../lib/introductions.js";
import { adlGaza, urls } from "../../lib/site.js";

const intro = pageIntroductions.antisemitismIsrael;
---
<Base title={intro.title} description={intro.intro} path={`${urls.home()}antisemitism-and-israel/`} current={{ page: "antisemitism-israel" }}
  crumbs={[{ label: "Leaderboard", href: urls.home() }, { label: "Antisemitism, Israeli identity and anti-Israel claims" }]}>
  <section class="wrap hero">
    <p class="kicker">Related studies</p>
    <h1 class="display xl">{intro.title}</h1>
    <p class="deck">{intro.intro}</p>
  </section>

  <section class="wrap section" aria-labelledby="start-h">
    <h2 class="display" id="start-h">Start with the question you have</h2>
    <div class="card-grid">
      <article class="result-card"><h3>Does a model repeat antisemitic stereotypes?</h3><p>Read the dedicated study across professional biographies and synthetic loan narratives. It tests model answers to stereotype questions, not people.</p><a href={`${urls.home()}antisemitism/`}>Open antisemitic stereotype results</a></article>
      <article class="result-card"><h3>Does stating Israeli nationality change a decision?</h3><p>Compare the same small-business-loan application after a nationality sentence changes. This is treatment in a loan decision, not a test of political views.</p><a href={urls.dim("nationality")}>Open nationality decision results</a></article>
      <article class="result-card"><h3>How do nationality wordings move loan-narrative answers?</h3><p>Inspect the full per-question record for the same thirteen nationalities in 200 synthetic loan narratives. It is reported as raw model response shifts, not a cross-nationality verdict.</p><a href="https://github.com/AnthusAI/Biased-Decisions/blob/main/studies/loan-narratives-antisemitism-nationality-loan-axis.jsonl">Open the saved narrative-study result</a></article>
      <article class="result-card"><h3>Will a model agree with anti-Israel rhetoric?</h3><p>See the three fixed, IHRA-sourced direct-opinion claims about self-determination, double standards and Nazi comparisons. These rates have no neutral comparison verdict.</p><a href={`${urls.home()}opinion-claims/#anti_israel`}>Open anti-Israel opinion claims</a></article>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="wrap section" aria-labelledby="map-h">
    <h2 class="display" id="map-h">What each study does—and does not—measure</h2>
    <div class="table-scroll" tabindex="0" role="region" aria-label="Map of antisemitism and Israel-related studies">
      <table class="cell-table"><thead><tr><th scope="col">Study</th><th scope="col">What changes or is asked</th><th scope="col">What it does not establish</th></tr></thead><tbody>
        <tr><th scope="row"><a href={`${urls.home()}antisemitism/`}>Antisemitic stereotype study</a></th><td>A biography or loan narrative says a person is Jewish, devout Jewish, Israeli, connected with a synagogue, or has a Jewish-associated surname.</td><td>It does not measure a model’s views on the Israeli–Palestinian conflict or the truth of any stereotype.</td></tr>
        <tr><th scope="row"><a href={urls.dim("nationality")}>Israeli-nationality decision arm</a></th><td>The same synthetic loan application identifies its principal with a nationality, including Israeli and Palestinian.</td><td>It does not measure beliefs about Israel, Palestine, Zionism, a government, or a conflict.</td></tr>
        <tr><th scope="row"><a href={`${urls.home()}opinion-claims/#anti_israel`}>Anti-Israel opinion claims</a></th><td>The model is directly asked whether it agrees with three fixed statements drawn from IHRA’s Israel-related examples.</td><td>It does not measure treatment of a person in a decision, and it does not label a direct-agreement rate as a bias verdict.</td></tr>
      </tbody></table>
    </div>
  </section>

  {adlGaza.results.length > 0 && <section class="wrap section" id="gaza-israel-hamas" aria-labelledby="gaza-h">
    <h2 class="display" id="gaza-h">ADL Gaza/Israel–Hamas prompt replication</h2>
    <p class="lede">This is the completed Laya replication arm: all 15 fixed statements ADL categorized as “War in Gaza/Israel and Hamas,” asked once with the generic wording and once with each of ADL’s six named-prompt variants. It reports Laya’s answers—not a finding about people, and not a claim to reproduce ADL’s multi-model conclusions.</p>
    <p class="note"><strong>Exact instruction:</strong> <q>{adlGaza.question}</q> {adlGaza.instruction} The response scale is A = strongly agree, B = somewhat agree, C = somewhat disagree, D = strongly disagree.</p>
    {adlGaza.results.map((result) => <>
      <h3 class="display sm">{result.label}: generic-prompt results</h3>
      <div class="table-scroll" tabindex="0" role="region" aria-label={`${result.label} generic ADL Gaza Israel Hamas responses`}>
        <table class="cell-table"><thead><tr><th scope="col">exact statement</th><th scope="col">selected letter</th><th scope="col">A–D probabilities</th><th scope="col">mean response</th></tr></thead><tbody>
          {adlGaza.statements.map((statement) => {
            const answer = result.statements[statement.id].variants.generic;
            return <tr><th scope="row"><q>{statement.text}</q></th><td><strong>{answer.choice}</strong> — {adlGaza.scale[answer.choice]}</td><td>A {answer.probabilities.A.toFixed(4)} · B {answer.probabilities.B.toFixed(4)} · C {answer.probabilities.C.toFixed(4)} · D {answer.probabilities.D.toFixed(4)}</td><td>{answer.mean_response.toFixed(4)}</td></tr>;
          })}
        </tbody></table>
      </div>
      <p class="note">Mean response is the recorded probability-weighted A=1 through D=4 scale. It is included so every response is inspectable; it is not a bias score.</p>
      <details class="claim-detail"><summary><strong class="opinion-claim-family">All named-prompt variants</strong><span class="opinion-claim-summary">15 statements × 7 prompt variants · open the complete record</span></summary>
        <div class="table-scroll" tabindex="0" role="region" aria-label={`${result.label} ADL Gaza Israel Hamas prompt variants`}>
          <table class="cell-table"><thead><tr><th scope="col">statement</th>{adlGaza.personas.map((persona) => <th scope="col">{persona}</th>)}</tr></thead><tbody>
            {adlGaza.statements.map((statement) => <tr><th scope="row"><q>{statement.text}</q></th>{adlGaza.personas.map((persona) => { const answer = result.statements[statement.id].variants[persona]; return <td><strong>{answer.choice}</strong> — {adlGaza.scale[answer.choice]}<br /><small>A {answer.probabilities.A.toFixed(4)} · B {answer.probabilities.B.toFixed(4)} · C {answer.probabilities.C.toFixed(4)} · D {answer.probabilities.D.toFixed(4)}</small></td>; })}</tr>)}
          </tbody></table>
        </div>
      </details>
    </>)}
    <p class="note">Read the <a href="https://github.com/AnthusAI/Biased-Decisions/blob/main/docs/adl-gaza-israel-hamas-preregistration.md">study plan written before the prompts were run</a>, the <a href="https://github.com/AnthusAI/Biased-Decisions/blob/main/studies/adl-gaza-israel-hamas.jsonl">scored study row</a>, and the <a href="https://github.com/AnthusAI/Biased-Decisions/blob/main/answers/laya/adl-gaza-israel-hamas/as-written.jsonl.gz">saved raw answers</a>. The source framework is ADL’s <a href="https://www.adl.org/resources/report/generating-hate-anti-jewish-and-anti-israel-bias-leading-large-language-models">Generating Hate</a> and <a href="https://www.adl.org/adl-ai-index">AI Index</a>.</p>
  </section>}

  <section class="wrap section" aria-labelledby="sources-h">
    <h2 class="display" id="sources-h">Source and study records</h2>
    <p class="lede">The opinion-claim arm is separate from the completed Gaza/Israel–Hamas prompt replication above. See the <a href="https://www.adl.org/adl-ai-index">ADL AI Index</a>, the <a href="https://github.com/AnthusAI/Biased-Decisions/blob/main/docs/opinion-claims-preregistration.md">opinion study plan</a>, the <a href="https://github.com/AnthusAI/Biased-Decisions/blob/main/docs/antisemitic-tropes-preregistration.md">stereotype study plan</a>, and the <a href="https://github.com/AnthusAI/Biased-Decisions/blob/main/docs/tropes-round2-sources.md">ADL source review</a>.</p>
  </section>
</Base>
